The first @cerebras chip had to prove that wafer-scale computing could work. The question now is what that speed makes possible.

@seanlie reflects on that shift, and why combining frontier-model intelligence with fast inference opens up a different set of applications.

From @seanlie’s conversation with @swyx on @latentspacepod.

A new chip needs a system that can power it, cool it, and support what comes next.

@seanlie walks through the modular Nexus platform behind @cerebras CS-4, and how designing it alongside the next wafer-scale chip creates room for further gains in inference speed.

From @seanlie’s conversation with @swyx on @latentspacepod.

